data affected_set_stop_line_note: String = "7933A temporary safety stop-line (operator recut calm-fox-44, 2026-08-06): when merge-base diff contains any non-docs .dag path, discovery skip admission must NOT skip dag_compile_clean_shard_a_witness_test.dag or dag_compile_clean_scope_witness_test.dag. This is a BROAD interim rule — not precise self-confirmation. It closes the #7915 failure mode (repair touched only dag/extdeps/systems/nvidia.dag and dag/test/claim/generated_artifact_drift_test.dag; import-closure never reached ci_layer_roots; shard_a was selection-skipped). Executable authority is ONE hand-Rust bridge in cli_run.rs (`cli_run_affected_set_stop_line_bridge` / `COMPILE_CLEAN_*_VALIDATING_ENTRY` consts) until 7933B lands (`gunbc.plans.affected_set_self_confirmation`). This carrier holds rationale and cost receipt only — no independently writable path rows (7933B introduces symbolic mechanism/check refs and host projection)."

data stop_line_cost_receipt_note: String = "Cost receipt (7933A broad rule, CI run 31132940985 / PR #7933 on srv_fleet_arm64): on this PR's broad diff the stop-line adds 0 marginal resolve/eval wall (scope witness entry observed ~17ms interpreted-leg eval, 01:00:33.514–01:00:33.531 UTC; shard_a entry not independently selection-skipped on this diff). On a narrow #7915-class diff where import-closure would skip both entries, bounded per-entry ceiling is enrolled witness_row_cost_basis entry wall: dag_compile_clean_scope_witness_test.dag 30550328673 ns (~30550 ms); shard_a entry includes bin_wet exemplar compile (compile_clean_shard_a_exemplar_compile_green) in the same cost class. Predicate: non-empty diff, not all docs/**, any .dag path; no mechanism roster. Executing control: cargo test -p v1-compiler --lib stop_line (cli_run.rs)."
